                            	  1474:     ; Submode 1.
                            	  1475:     ; Copies the whole play area to NT 0, one row each frame.
                            	  1476:     ;
                            	  1477:     ; TODO:
                            	  1478:     ; If mode 7 scrolls to a dark room, then it sets
                            	  1479:     ; CurRow to zero. Otherwise it would be $FF.
                            	  1480:     ; A positive value triggers this submode 1 to transfer
                            	  1481:     ; the whole play area.
                            	  1482:     ;
                            	  1483:     ; But why? As far as I can tell, the NT 0 is already in
                            	  1484:     ; a good state reflecting the new room. The only thing
                            	  1485:     ; needed is possibly to brighten the room by way of
                            	  1486:     ; changing the palette.
                            	  1487:     ;
                            	  1488:     ; So why does mode 7 trigger this?
                            	  1489:     ; Is there another mode that truly needs this behavior?
                            	  1490:     ;
02:00030DD6 102C00E9        	  1491:     move.b  ($00E9,A4),D0
02:00030DDA 6B06            	  1492:     bmi  _anon_z05_40
02:00030DDC 6100348E        	  1493:     jsr     CopyNextRowToTransferBuf
